WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.052
Let’s review the major patterns.

00:00:02.052 --> 00:00:08.422
Method chaining connects transformations. Pivot tables summarize across categories.

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:12.007
Melt reshapes wide data to long format.

00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:15.342
Datetime tools create time features.

00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:18.247
Rolling windows summarize trends.

00:00:18.247 --> 00:00:26.866
Mapping translates categories, join indicators help validate merges, and functions package workflows for reuse.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:34.440
The larger goal is to make complex table transformations readable, testable, and repeatable.

00:00:34.936 --> 00:00:42.623
Module 12 shifts the focus from transforming data to checking whether the data is actually ready for analysis.

00:00:42.623 --> 00:00:51.738
We’ll work with missing values, duplicates, incorrect data types, inconsistent categories, possible outliers,

00:00:51.738 --> 00:00:58.744
and exploratory summaries. The goal is to understand the dataset before trusting any result from it.
